1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,650
In a series circuit, components are connected end to end in a single loop, like a one-lane road.

2
00:00:05,650 --> 00:00:11,709
The current is the same at every point, but the voltage from the cell is shared between the components.

3
00:00:11,709 --> 00:00:14,097
With two identical lamps, each gets half.

4
00:00:15,155 --> 00:00:21,388
Add a third lamp and the voltage is shared even more, so all the lamps get dimmer. And if one lamp breaks,

5
00:00:21,388 --> 00:00:27,330
the only path is broken, so every lamp goes out, just like traffic stopping on a closed one-lane road.

6
00:00:28,388 --> 00:00:33,223
To measure current, connect an ammeter in series, so the current flows through it.

7
00:00:33,223 --> 00:00:37,534
To measure voltage, connect a voltmeter in parallel, across the component.
